<title>USA: TSI Inc receives $1.3 mln military order.</title>
<headline>TSI Inc receives $1.3 mln military order.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PAUL, Minn. 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>TSI Inc said Monday it has received a $1.3 million order from the U.S. Department of Defense for 244 additional Portacount Respirator Fit testers.</p>
<p>The testers are used to help protect personnel from dangerous airborne substances and were purchased primarily for use by the U.S. Air Force.</p>
<p>&quot;This addition to our U.S. defense contract is a nice boost for our fiscal 1997 fourth quarter ending March 31, 1997,&quot; Leroy Fingerson, chairman of the measuring instrument maker said in a news release.</p>
<p>--Reuters Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
